.TH CHTTPSVR_REQ_QUERY_OOM 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
chttpsvr_req_query_oom \- check whether chttpsvr_req_query ran out of memory
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <chttpserver.h>

bool chttpsvr_req_query_oom(const chttpsvr_req *req);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Returns true if a query-string allocation for this request has failed
under OOM: either chttpsvr_req_query's own result-array growth, or the
one-time, shared query-string parse that chttpsvr_req_query and
chttpsvr_req_query_one each lazily trigger on first use.

chttpsvr_req_query returns (NULL, count=0) both when the requested key
is absent and when an OOM condition prevents building the result array.
Use this function to distinguish the two cases after any NULL return
from chttpsvr_req_query.

The flag is latching: once set it remains true for the remainder of the
request regardless of subsequent query calls.  Returns false when req is
NULL.
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
true; a query-string allocation for this request failed under OOM.
false; no allocation error occurred (or req is NULL).
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR chttpsvr_req_query (3),
.BR chttpsvr_req_query_one (3)
